---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Complete Guide to Ad Policy & Landing Page Compliance | PixelPage Blog"
  description="Avoid account suspensions and rejected ads. Learn how automated compliance scanning catches misleading claims, false scarcity, and policy risks."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 bg-[#0d0d14]">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <a href="/blog" class="text-xs font-semibold text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 flex items-center gap-1 mb-4">
          <span>← Back to Blog Overview</span>
        </a>
        <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold tracking-wider px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30">
          Ad Compliance
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mt-4 mb-4 leading-tight font-sans">
          The Complete Guide to Ad Policy & Landing Page Compliance
        </h1>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-xs text-gray-400 pb-6 border-b border-white/10">
          <span>By Compliance AI Team</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>July 19, 2026</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>7 min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-base text-gray-200 leading-relaxed font-semibold">
          Getting a client's Meta Business Manager or Google Ads account suspended due to landing page compliance violations is every performance marketer's worst nightmare.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">1. Common Landing Page Red Flags</h2>
        <p>
          Ad networks use sophisticated web crawlers to audit destination URLs. The most frequent policy triggers include:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300">
          <li><strong>Unsubstantiated Guarantees:</strong> Claims like "Guaranteed 10x ROI in 30 days" without explicit disclaimers.</li>
          <li><strong>False Scarcity & Countdown Timers:</strong> Dynamic countdown timers that reset on refresh are flagged as misleading.</li>
          <li><strong>Mismatched Destination Copy:</strong> When the ad headline promises one offer, but the landing page displays different pricing or terms.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">2. Automated Compliance Checking with PixelPage AI</h2>
        <p>
          Instead of manually checking compliance rules before pushing ad campaigns live, PixelPage incorporates an automated Compliance Review Agent into every page build pipeline.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-[#161622] border border-violet-500/30 p-6 rounded-2xl space-y-3 my-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-violet-300">🛡️ Real-Time Policy Risk Scanning</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
            PixelPage evaluates copy against Meta Advertising Standards and Google Ads Policies, flagging potential violations in a real-time compliance banner so you can edit risk factors before launching.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-6">
          <a
            href="/chat"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-bold text-xs bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-500 text-white shadow-lg shadow-violet-500/25 hover:opacity-95 transition-all"
          >
            <span>Try PixelPage Studio Free →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
